# Partner ad rotator

When editing partner ads or dropping a unit on a page:

1. **Copy/config** lives in `src/lib/partner-ads.ts` (`partnerAds(placement)`). Take the words from MyOMR’s ad registry. Do not put headlines, URLs, or themes in the carousel. A photo record adds `image`, `ink`, `accent`, and at least three `lines` (`photoLabel`, `offer`, `support`, `photoCta`, `ctaShort`). The rotator shows the next line the next time that advertiser appears. The photo layout turns on only when those are set (`isPartnerPhotoAd`). `headline`, `body`, and `cta` stay for the gradient banner. One shared layout — do not add a theme-specific photo skin. The offer is bold Geist on a white card, with an outline pill, matching the Moneycontrol native unit. A finished image file is **not** a rotator slide and is **not** pinned to one page. The pool is `PARTNER_ARTWORK_SOURCES`. `<LayoutImageBanner placement="…" />` picks with `layoutBannerForView(sessionSeed, pathname)`: one file for that visitor on that page, a different file on the next page or the next visit. Do not lay offer text on the file.
2. **UI:** `<PageAdSlot shape="square|rectangle" placement="…" />` is the native photo rotator only. Finished images sit in existing columns (job rail, jobs hub, looking-for-work, news sidebar, article sidebar, event rail, classified rail, directory listing) and in `<SiteWideAdBand />` on pages that have no column.
3. **UTMs:** `utm_source=mychennaicity`, `utm_medium=referral`, `utm_campaign=partner_ad`, `utm_content=<placement>`.
4. Update `hasDedicatedPartnerAdSlot()` / `shouldShowSiteWideAd()` when you add a new inline slot so the site-wide band does not double up.
5. This is **not** IAB `src/ads/` (`AdSlot` — do not remount on public pages) and **not** `AdvertisePanel` (sell-side). `ArticleAdRegion` is AdSense-only.
6. **Clicks:** keep `data-partner-id` and `data-utm-content` on the rotator link. Super admin reads those as banner clicks (SOP O item 6). Dot buttons are not clicks.

SOP K in `docs/AGENT_LEARNINGS_AND_SOPS.md`.
